  "hints": [
    "Use a Python list as a LIFO stack: push opening brackets \"(\", \"[\", \"{\".",
    "Whenever you encounter a closing bracket, check that the stack is non-empty AND its top element matches the expected opener; ignore non-bracket characters.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  pairs = {\")\": \"(\", \"]\": \"[\", \"}\": \"{\"}\n  stack = []\n  for ch in expr:\n      if ch in \"([{\": stack.append(ch)\n      elif ch in pairs:\n          if not stack or stack.pop() != pairs[ch]: return False\n  return len(stack) == 0"
  ],
